      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not all people uses Turbo Switcher Pro, but big world builders use this tool because it saves a lot worktime. \nNow it has still SDK detection issue where it still thinks i have Android build mode but Builder showed clearly i have Windows build.\nIt's kinda annoying detection bug. Only if i restart Unity again, the bug disappear and it detect correctly i have Windows build.\nThe bug seems come back if i work for long time at Unity project, after switch from Android to Windows.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-08T14:46:20.890Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Some users have switching tool Turbo Switcher Pro (TPS) to switch between Windows and Android side.\nBut for some reason, SDK didn't detect well at Windows side and STILL report world is too big with over 50MB size.\nPlease add extra checks in SDK to reduce wrong errors while world publishing.\nSometimes i need restart or switch to fix this bug. It's kinda stupid bug.\n\nThe bug is already seen in older SDKs and even it still exists in last SDK build for 2019.4.31f1, so i guess it has same code to check the world size and which side it is.",
